 direct democracy and a  common sense of national identity as  ways of creating a more just society  where people live together but also help  each other and treat each other fairly  Russo's ideas were extremely influential  in the 18th century and they had a  massive impact on the French Revolution  and other historical movements that  wanted to do away with absolutism and  establish a more democratic system of  government but unlike Rousseau other  political thinkers who came after him  did advocate for the abolishing of  private property and the complete  overthrow of the current economic system  this includes Karl Marx Friedrich Engels  and other thinkers that we have come to  associate with the ideology of communism  people like Marx argued that we could  not create a more fair and just society  unless the existing economic structure  was done away with completely and this  includes abolishing private property as  we know it without getting too much into  Marx's historical materialism it is  sufficient to say that Marx believed in  the concept of class struggle the idea  that there are two main classes of  people in modern capitalist societies  the poor majority known as the  proletariat and the rich minority known  as the bourgeoisie according to Marx the  rich minority is exploiting the poor  majority and these poor workers have  become alienated from the products that  they produce from the act of production  itself from other workers and even from  their very essence as human beings  eventually the poor majority will rise  up overthrow the wealthy bourgeoisie and  all private property will be replaced  with communal property this will lead to  true equality and eventually class  distinctions and even national  boundaries will wither away as people  learn to live together in communal  harmony after Marx's death communist  revolutionaries like Vladimir Lenin in  Russia took inspiration from Marx but  they also modified his philosophy to fit  their own needs and circumstances they  sought to put Marx's ideas about  overthrowing the bourgeoisie into  practice and in the pursuit of this goal  they were willing to do rat  things and this includes killing many  innocent people who just happened to  have been born into the upper echelon of  society or who happen to oppose the  ideology of Lenin and the Bolsheviks the  Bolsheviks were willing to kill innocent  people in the name of what they  considered to be a greater goal what  they saw as the greater good of  establishing a classless communist  Society and look no further than the  fate of the Romanov children if you want  to know just how far these communist  revolutionaries were willing to go  tsukasa shares some clear parallels with  this type of revolutionary radicalism  like Rousseau tsukasa believes that  society corrupts human beings and  because they lived in this corrupt  society for a longer period of time  adults are more corrupt than the youth  for this reason in order to create a  more just and fair society tsukasa  believes that we need to start anew and  we must start with the youth who have  not yet been fully corrupted by the  evils of modern society Rousseau never  believed that this type of return to a  more pure existence was possible and he  did not advocate for it but Tsukasa  seized the stone world as the perfect  opportunity to do just that  furthermore like the radical  revolutionaries of the past  Tsukasa is willing to commit radical  acts of violence in the name of his  cause Tsukasa  is willing to end the lives of millions  of adults regardless of whether or not  they are good people because he believes  that the greater good of establishing a  more pure and just society justifies  this sacrifice sanku disagrees of course  and the battle between sanku scientific  genius and tsukasa's physical prowess  also becomes a battle between sank whose  pragmatic conservatism and tsukasa's  revolutionary radicalism I find this  conflict to be absolutely fascinating  and even though I side with sanku and I  can't possibly support Lucas's actions I  am intrigued by tsukasa's philosophy the  petrification that lasted 3,700 years  completely changed the world and these  radically different circumstances  inspired Tsukasa to embrace radical  action in order to create what he  believes to be a new and better world we  can all agree that modern society has  too much corruption and injustice so we  can see where Tsukasa is coming from  even if we reject his methods just like  we can agree with Light Yagami that the  world has to  crime and evil even if we don't support  his mass-murdering methods and this is  precisely what makes for a great anime  conflict even if you reject the villains  methods you can still understand that  perhaps even relate to some of the  villains motivations this type of  conflict makes you think it makes you  re-evaluate your own positions and it  makes you wonder what you would do if  you suddenly found yourself in such a  radically different situation and I love  that in an anime I really enjoy anime  series that put so much thought into  their conflicts and these are the types  of stories that really stick with me  whether it's Psychopaths Code Geass  Death Note Full Metal Alchemist  Brotherhood or dr. stone I love an anime  that makes me think about politics  philosophy and the pros and cons of  modern society dr. stone really is  deeper than it appears at first glance  and I can't wait to learn more about  this stone world and the apocalyptic  philosophy that lies just beneath the  Shonan surface if you enjoyed this video  you want to see more videos like this  one you can leave a like to let me know  and if you're new to anime uproar please  don't forget to subscribe and hit that  notification bell I want to give a huge  thank you to all of our anime upper  patrons for supporting our work and  making our work possible a special thank  you to all of our pro hero tier patrons  including the one and only Gilgamesh  nothing but a fan Jason Wilson Kings  eldress and on hell crews another  massive thank you to our the one tier  patrons the ones who stand above all  other clans including baby ray ace  ingrid ah al Olin Adam Maddy Mac  makoto-kun  and keelon and finally at the very  pinnacle of interdimensional greatness a  tier reserved only for legends a massive  thank you to Reagan Harrison and Lord  naksan or disciples Oh Lord to ego  himself if you feel that our content  provides value for you when you want to  support more be sure to check out our  patreon link in the description even a  single dollar will give you access to  our patron exclusive discord and your  name will appear in our videos along  with these amazing people as always  thank you guys so much for watching  and until next time see our space  cowboys  [Music]
 

